      "role": "user",
      "content": "it says \"generally considered successful\" but i feel like some of my profs talk about it like it was a disaster for the middle class. like, isn't the whole \"growth\" argument kind of a stretch when you look at how much inequality shot up during that time? is there an actual consensus on that part or is it just a matter of opinion?",
